From 8e3e3addefde7b7f2d62ec54abe16a68186645d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nigel Todman <veritas@vts-tech.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:33:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FOV slider: match the menu text size, widen range to 64-128

Two fixes to the in-game FOV slider from the previous batch:

- Range 60-110 -> 64-128 (default 90 = vanilla).  Step is 2 degrees
  so 90 is exactly reachable (64 + 13*2 = 90; 90 + 19*2 = 128); the
  thermometer (doom/strife) and slider knob (heretic/hexen) map
  (fov-64)/4 into 17 cells, and the handlers clamp hand-edited
  config values to the bounds instead of stepping past them.
- The FOV menu text no longer looks smaller than the rest.  In doom
  and strife the label is the small font scaled (nearest neighbour)
  to the height of the M_* menu patches - the SOUND row height for
  the label, the HIGH/LOW patch height for the value - so the FOV
  row matches the other options rows (measured on doom1.wad: labels
  15px, values 12px, the small font 7px at 1x, same red ramp).
  Heretic/hexen already draw it with the big menu font.
- The non-default projection now computes the half-angle tangent
  directly: the old finetangent-table lookup truncated to the
  fine-angle grid (up to ~0.2 degrees off); the direct tangent is
  exact at every value.  At fov 90 the vanilla expression stays
  bit-identical (the if-branch is untouched).

Verified: 39/39 logic checks against the real tables.c finetangent
data and the real FixedDiv (grid hits 90/128 exactly; dot in [0,16]
for width 17; hand-edited values clamp; every grid value renders at
its exact FOV < 0.01 deg; psprite guard semantics; weapon scale
1.600/0.488 at 64/128 degrees); full autotools build green for all
four games + setup + server, --version = "Chocolate Doom VK 3.0.0"
on all six; menu layout mocked against real doom1.wad lumps.
